ty. It was one of the two basic EASEP experiments. Its sensors did not measure Earth–Moon distance. The Laser Ranging Retroreflector returned laser pulses sent from Earth. Timing the round trip enabled precise measurements of Earth–Moon distance. The reflector did not generate the laser beam. Apollo 11 carried EASEP, the Early Apollo Scientific Experiments Package: PSEP and LRRR were its two basic experiments. Later missions carried the expanded ALSEP. A separate solar-wind composition experiment also flew on Apollo 11. There was no lunar rover on this mission."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","Instruments and experiments",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_8_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_8_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Scientific sources"],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"10",". ","Scientific observations"],["P",{},"Apollo 11 carried EASEP, the Early Apollo Scientific Experiments Package: PSEP and LRRR were its two basic experiments. Later missions carried the expanded ALSEP. A separate solar-wind composition experiment also flew on Apollo 11. There was no lunar rover on this mission. After landing and surface exploration, Eagle’s ascent stage lifted off. It rendezvoused and docked with Columbia in lunar orbit. Armstrong, Aldrin and the samples transferred to Columbia; the ascent stage was later jettisoned. The crew returned to Earth in Columbia’s command module. Images from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter Camera show the Apollo 11 descent stage and the trails left by the astronauts. The object left at the landing site was not the cabin that carried them back to orbit."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["S