{"type":"frame-snapshot","snapshot":{"callId":"zyfb@331","phase":"after","pageId":"page@1045ab9c9d282078e817d8ffc70b07a5","frameId":"frame@3da48dae09ef59b907e8d12e7f09cec2","frameUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:4173/","doctype":"html","html":["HTML",{"lang":"en"},[[13,9]],[[16,19]],["BODY",{},[[16,20]],["DIV",{"id":"root"},["DIV",{"class":"app-shell","data-reduced-motion":"true"},[[16,22]],[[12,2]],["MAIN",{"id":"main","class":"main-content "},["SECTION",{"class":"interior-screen"},[[13,11]],[[13,14]],[[13,16]],["DIV",{"class":"universe"},["LABEL",{},[[11,0]],["SELECT",{"__playwright_target__":""},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"apollo-11"},[[11,1]]],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"near-shoemaker"},[[11,3]]],[[11,6]]]],[[11,10]],[[11,12]],[[11,14]],["H2",{},"NEAR SHOEMAKER",[[11,16]]],["DIV",{"class":"archive-topics"},["DETAILS",{"open":""},[[4,0]],["P",{},"Six investigations connect the journey, the rock and the decision to land."],[[11,63]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,65]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,93]],["P",{},"The Discovery mission set out to rendezvous with an asteroid and investigate its physical properties. A flyby of Mathilde and Earth gravity assist preceded the Eros encounter. The aborted 1998 maneuver forced a revised route and delayed orbital arrival."],[[11,135]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,137]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,165]],[[11,167]],[[11,207]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,209]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,237]],["P",{},"NASA funded the mission and Johns Hopkins APL built and operated the spacecraft. Thomas Coughlin, Robert Farquhar and Andrew Cheng held the historical project-manager, mission-manager and project-scientist roles described by APL."],[[11,279]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,281]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,294]],[[11,296]],[[11,336]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,338]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,366]],["P",{},"NASA lists a launch mass of 805 kilograms. Four solar arrays powered the spacecraft. Imaging, infrared spectroscopy, X-ray/gamma-ray spectroscopy, laser ranging, magnetic measurements and radio tracking supplied complementary observations. No purpose-built landing legs were carried."],[[11,408]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,410]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,438]],["P",{},"NASA lists a launch mass of 805 kilograms. Four solar arrays powered the spacecraft. Imaging, infrared spectroscopy, X-ray/gamma-ray spectroscopy, laser ranging, magnetic measurements and radio tracking supplied complementary observations. No purpose-built landing legs were carried."],[[11,480]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,482]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,495]],[[11,497]],[[11,537]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,539]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,567]],["P",{},"The Multi-Spectral Imager mapped morphology and colour differences. The Near Infrared Spectrometer measured reflected infrared light to investigate minerals. A May 2000 power problem ended NIS operations. X-ray/gamma-ray spectroscopy probes elemental composition. The laser rangefinder measures distance for shape and topography. The magnetometer investigates magnetic fields. Radio tracking constrains motion, gravity and mass distribution."],[[11,609]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,611]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,639]],["P",{},"NASA describes touchdown south of the saddle-shaped Himeros region. The official landing-site mosaic shows the planned site with south toward the top. The orbiter survived touchdown. On February 14 NASA announced an extension for gamma-ray measurements and prioritised their recovery over other recorder data using the reliable low-gain link. Last contact was February 28, 2001. NEAR established asteroid orbiting and landing milestones and left a record of images, spectra, ranging and tracking for later study."],[[11,681]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,683]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,711]],["P",{},"The Discovery mission set out to rendezvous with an asteroid and investigate its physical properties. A flyby of Mathilde and Earth gravity assist preceded the Eros encounter. The aborted 1998 maneuver forced a revised route and delayed orbital arrival."],[[11,753]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,755]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,783]],["P",{},"The orbiter survived touchdown. On February 14 NASA announced an extension for gamma-ray measurements and prioritised their recovery over other recorder data using the reliable low-gain link. Last contact was February 28, 2001. NEAR established asteroid orbiting and landing milestones and left a record of images, spectra, ranging and tracking for later study."],[[11,825]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,827]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,855]],["P",{},"The landing was a choice. The next signal was an opportunity."],[[11,897]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,899]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,927]],["P",{},"Orbital insertion was February 14, 2000. The deliberate controlled descent reached Eros on February 12, 2001. Surviving communications enabled surface gamma-ray work; last contact was February 28. This was a planned descent by an orbiter, not an accidental crash."],[[11,969]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,971]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,999]],["P",{},"Orbital insertion was February 14, 2000. The deliberate controlled descent reached Eros on February 12, 2001. Surviving communications enabled surface gamma-ray work; last contact was February 28. This was a planned descent by an orbiter, not an accidental crash."],[[11,1041]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1043]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1071]],["P",{},"You followed a spacecraft to a target that would not stand still, then learned why staying beside it required careful measurement. The team brought an orbiter down slowly. When it survived, they made room for another question about the rock beneath it. NEAR stayed on Eros. Its measurements travelled home."],[[11,1113]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1115]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1143]],["P",{},"The NASA Eros STL preserves an irregular shape without photographic textures. The official NASA/JPL/JHUAPL planned landing-site mosaic has south toward the top. It supplies regional context; our mesh has no validated geographic registration."],[[11,1185]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1187]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1215]],[[11,1217]],[[11,1257]],["DETAILS",{},[[11,1259]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA NEAR model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/asteroid-433-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA Eros shape"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"]]]]]],["H2",{},"Full mission reference chapters"],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"A rendezvous takes more than a straight line"],["P",{},"NEAR launched on February 17, 1996, passed Mathilde on June 27, 1997 and used an Earth gravity assist on January 23, 1998. A near-Earth asteroid follows a solar orbit that brings it into the neighbourhood of Earth; it does not mean an impact is imminent. Navigation changes the spacecraft trajectory to meet a moving target. Mathilde was a flyby; Eros was the rendezvous objective."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","A rendezvous takes more than a straight line",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_t_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_t_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Scientific sources"],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"The meeting that had to wait"],["P",{},"An aborted December 20, 1998 engine burn prevented the intended rendezvous. A December 23 flyby gathered observations before a revised trajectory brought NEAR back in 2000. A flyby passes a target. Rendezvous reduces relative motion enough to stay nearby."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","The meeting that had to wait",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_u_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_u_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Scientific sources"],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Not a small planet"],["P",{},"The real Eros shape is elongated and irregular. The supplied NASA STL preserves surface relief but contains no photographic texture, geographic axes or longitude labels. Rotate the body to compare silhouettes. Shape alone cannot identify mineral composition or justify naming an unregistered crater."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","Not a small planet",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"