st flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,93]],["P",{},"Ingenuity travelled beneath Perseverance as a technology demonstrator. It was meant to test controlled flight, not to duplicate the rover’s science laboratory. Demonstrating flight opened a later role in aerial reconnaissance."],[[21,135]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,137]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,165]],["P",{},"The original objective was to demonstrate powered, controlled flight in the Martian atmosphere. The planned five-flight experiment grew into operations demonstrations and further engineering tests. Its cameras supplied navigation observations and aerial imagery; it did not carry a Perseverance-style scientific instrument payload."],[[21,207]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,209]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,237]],["P",{},"NASA JPL led the helicopter effort with contributions from AeroVironment, SolAero, NASA Ames and NASA Langley. The mission reference below distinguishes historical team roles from a current staff directory."],[[21,279]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,281]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,294]],[[21,296]],[[21,336]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,338]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,366]],["P",{},"Two counter-rotating rotor levels, a solar array, battery-powered systems and four landing legs supported autonomous flight and survival. The initial plan allowed up to five demonstration flights; the completed flight record reached 72. Onboard camera observations and sensors supported navigation; there was no science laboratory payload."],[[21,408]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,410]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,438]],["P",{},"Two counter-rotating rotor levels, a solar array, battery-powered systems and four landing legs supported autonomous flight and survival. The initial plan allowed up to five demonstration flights; the completed flight record reached 72. Onboard camera observations and sensors supported navigation; there was no science laboratory payload."],[[21,480]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,482]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,495]],[[21,497]],[[21,537]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,539]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,567]],["P",{},"Mars has roughly one percent of Earth’s atmospheric density near the surface. Rotors have much less air to push against. Lower gravity reduces the aircraft’s weight, but does not remove the need to generate lift. The solar array above the rotors charges the lithium-ion battery system. Stored energy powers flight, electronics and heaters. Sunlight is a source; the battery stores energy for use when the panel is not producing it."],[[21,609]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,611]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,639]],["P",{},"Flight 72 was intended as a brief vertical flight to check systems and photograph the area after the preceding flight ended early. Ingenuity climbed to its planned height and began descending. Communications were lost near the end of the flight. Communications were reestablished the following day. Later imagery showed rotor-blade damage that ended Ingenuity’s ability to fly. The images establish damage; they do not provide a complete eyewitness view of touchdown. NASA’s investigation linked too few trackable surface features to unreliable motion estimates. Its most-likely scenario involved excessive horizontal motion, a hard impact on a sand-ripple slope, rapid changes in attitude and damaging rotor loads."],[[21,681]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,683]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,711]],["P",{},"Thin air made lift difficult. Nights required energy and thermal protection. Interplanetary communications made onboard control essential. Visual navigation relied on useful ground features. The evidence records explain how each challenge influenced design or operations; no single engineering choice solved all of them."],[[21,753]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,755]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,783]],["P",{},"Communications were reestablished the following day. Later imagery showed rotor-blade damage that ended Ingenuity’s ability to fly. The images establish damage; they do not provide a complete eyewitness view of touchdown. NASA’s investigation linked too few trackable surface features to unreliable motion estimates. Its most-likely scenario involved excessive horizontal motion, a hard impact on a sand-ripple slope, rapid changes in attitude and damaging rotor loads."],[[21,825]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,827]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,855]],["P",{},"Five were the plan. The rest changed what engineers could ask for next."],[[21,897]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,899]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,927]],["P",{},"Flight 72 on January 18, 2024 was the final flight. NASA announced the end of the flight mission on January 25. A later investigation described the most-likely accident sequence while acknowledging uncertainty. The flight data, operational experience and limits that engineers identified remain useful for designing future aerial explorers."],[[21,969]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,971]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,999]],["P",{},"Flight 72 on January 18, 2024 was the last flight. NASA’s January mission-end announcement and its December investigation account are separate events. Damaged blades were observed; the detailed accident chain remains a most-likely reconstruction rather than an eyewitness record."],[[21,1041]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,1043]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,1071]],["P",{},"The first question was whether a small helicopter could fly on Mars at all. You followed the air, the energy and the decisions that made the answer possible. Ingenuity went on to offer another view of the ground: one that could help a rover team decide where to look and how to get there. The experiment had become useful in ways a short first hop could only suggest. The final flight left damaged blades and an incomplete view of the landing. Engineers built the best explanation the evidence allowed, and kept the uncertainty visible. That is part of the work, too. Ingenuity will not take off again. The next aircraft can still learn from every flight it made."],[[21,1113]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,1115]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survives-first-cold-martian-night-on-its-own/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Surviving the first night alone"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-helicopters-solar-array-as-seen-by-perseverances-mastcam-z/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Solar array and stored energy"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/what-were-learning-about-ingenuitys-flight-control-and-aerodynamic-performance/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Flight control and aerodynamic performance"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/planets/mars/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-reaches-a-total-of-30-minutes-aloft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,1143]],["P",{},"Original rotor, energy and terrain-observation drawings are teaching illustrations. The official flight log and NASA/JPL flight-map references provide the historical context. Our globe does not invent geographic tracks between flights."],[[21,1185]],["DETAILS",{},[[21,1187]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopen