{"type":"frame-snapshot","snapshot":{"callId":"zyfb@347","phase":"after","pageId":"page@1045ab9c9d282078e817d8ffc70b07a5","frameId":"frame@3da48dae09ef59b907e8d12e7f09cec2","frameUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:4173/","doctype":"html","html":["HTML",{"lang":"en"},[[33,9]],[[36,19]],["BODY",{},[[36,20]],["DIV",{"id":"root"},["DIV",{"class":"app-shell","data-reduced-motion":"true"},[[36,22]],[[32,2]],["MAIN",{"id":"main","class":"main-content "},["SECTION",{"class":"interior-screen"},[[33,11]],[[33,14]],[[33,16]],["DIV",{"class":"universe"},["LABEL",{},[[31,0]],["SELECT",{"__playwright_target__":""},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"apollo-11"},[[31,1]]],[[10,0]],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"ingenuity"},[[31,5]]]]],[[31,10]],[[31,12]],[[31,14]],["H2",{},"APOLLO 11",[[31,16]]],["DIV",{"class":"archive-topics"},["DETAILS",{"open":""},[[4,0]],["P",{},"Five investigations. Inspect the hardware, collect the records, and reconstruct the journey home."],[[31,63]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,65]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,93]],["P",{},"Apollo 11 followed earlier Apollo tests of spacecraft, lunar navigation and rendezvous. Its objective combined landing people on the Moon with returning them safely. Earlier missions reduced risk; they did not remove the uncertainties of the first landing."],[[31,135]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,137]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,165]],["P",{},"Land a crew, conduct surface exploration and return safely; use the two-stage lander and lunar rendezvous to achieve that objective."],[[31,207]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,209]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,237]],["P",{},"Neil Armstrong commanded Apollo 11, Buzz Aldrin piloted the Lunar Module and Michael Collins piloted Columbia. NASA launch, flight-control, engineering and science teams supported the crew. The separate orbital and surface roles were essential to the rendezvous plan."],[[31,279]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,281]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,294]],[[31,296]],[[31,336]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,338]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,366]],["P",{},"Eagle had two stages with separate propulsion roles. Four landing legs supported the descent stage; the ascent stage carried the cabin and return-to-orbit engine. The mission lasted 8 days, 3 hours, 18 minutes and 35 seconds according to NASA’s overview. Display model dimensions are not engineering measurements."],[[31,408]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,410]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,438]],["P",{},"Eagle had two stages with separate propulsion roles. Four landing legs supported the descent stage; the ascent stage carried the cabin and return-to-orbit engine. The mission lasted 8 days, 3 hours, 18 minutes and 35 seconds according to NASA’s overview. Display model dimensions are not engineering measurements."],[[31,480]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,482]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,495]],[[31,497]],[[31,537]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,539]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,567]],["P",{},"The Passive Seismic Experiment Package measured ground vibrations, including signals used to investigate lunar seismic activity. It was one of the two basic EASEP experiments. Its sensors did not measure Earth–Moon distance. The Laser Ranging Retroreflector returned laser pulses sent from Earth. Timing the round trip enabled precise measurements of Earth–Moon distance. The reflector did not generate the laser beam. Apollo 11 carried EASEP, the Early Apollo Scientific Experiments Package: PSEP and LRRR were its two basic experiments. Later missions carried the expanded ALSEP. A separate solar-wind composition experiment also flew on Apollo 11. There was no lunar rover on this mission."],[[31,609]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,611]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,639]],["P",{},"Apollo 11 carried EASEP, the Early Apollo Scientific Experiments Package: PSEP and LRRR were its two basic experiments. Later missions carried the expanded ALSEP. A separate solar-wind composition experiment also flew on Apollo 11. There was no lunar rover on this mission. After landing and surface exploration, Eagle’s ascent stage lifted off. It rendezvoused and docked with Columbia in lunar orbit. Armstrong, Aldrin and the samples transferred to Columbia; the ascent stage was later jettisoned. The crew returned to Earth in Columbia’s command module. Images from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter Camera show the Apollo 11 descent stage and the trails left by the astronauts. The object left at the landing site was not the cabin that carried them back to orbit."],[[31,681]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,683]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,711]],["P",{},"Apollo 11 followed earlier Apollo tests of spacecraft, lunar navigation and rendezvous. Its objective combined landing people on the Moon with returning them safely. Earlier missions reduced risk; they did not remove the uncertainties of the first landing."],[[31,753]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,755]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,783]],["P",{},"After landing and surface exploration, Eagle’s ascent stage lifted off. It rendezvoused and docked with Columbia in lunar orbit. Armstrong, Aldrin and the samples transferred to Columbia; the ascent stage was later jettisoned. The crew returned to Earth in Columbia’s command module. Images from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter Camera show the Apollo 11 descent stage and the trails left by the astronauts. The object left at the landing site was not the cabin that carried them back to orbit."],[[31,825]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,827]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,855]],["P",{},"That was how it was meant to work."],[[31,897]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,899]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,927]],["P",{},"Landing was July 20, 1969; the EVA and EASEP deployment occurred July 21 UTC. Ascent and docking followed on July 21. Earth departure was July 22 UTC and splashdown July 24. UTC dates avoid mixing a US evening with the next calendar day in universal time."],[[31,969]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,971]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,999]],["P",{},"Landing was July 20, 1969; the EVA and EASEP deployment occurred July 21 UTC. Ascent and docking followed on July 21. Earth departure was July 22 UTC and splashdown July 24. UTC dates avoid mixing a US evening with the next calendar day in universal time."],[[31,1041]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,1043]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,1071]],["P",{},"The descent stage had landed them safely and given the ascent stage a place to leave from. Its journey ended at Tranquility Base. The crew's did not. Armstrong and Aldrin carried samples back to Columbia. The experiments they deployed opened other ways to study the Moon: ground vibrations, and light returned to Earth. Decades later, an orbiting camera could still pick out the landing stage. A machine no longer flying, still part of the record."],[[31,1113]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,1115]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Landing gear technical report"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ochmo-tb-022-apollo-lunar-lander.pdf#page=6","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar lander human factors, p. 6 (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/50-years-ago-one-small-step-one-giant-leap/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 surface experiments"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Apollo_11.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 press kit (PDF)"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-11-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 landing site, LROC"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,1143]],["P",{},"Original seismic and laser diagrams explain measurement concepts. NASA’s LRO landing-site reference provides observed imagery of the descent stage and surface traces. The global Moon view uses NASA’s LRO-based CGI map, an aesthetically processed visualization product, not a surveyed surface reconstruction."],[[31,1185]],["DETAILS",{},[[31,1187]],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollos-lunar-module-bridged-technological-leap-to-the-moon/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Lunar Module engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/history/apollo-11-mission-overview/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Apollo 11 mission overview"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720018253","target":"_bla